<title>MALAYSIA: Kemayan says to develop land in Johor.</title>
<headline>Kemayan says to develop land in Johor.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kemayan Corp Bhd said its subsidiary company has entered into an agreement to jointly develop 241.2 acres of land in southern Johor state into a residential and commercial project.</p>
<p>In a statement, the commodities and property firm said its unit, Binabaik Construction Management Sdn Bhd, has signed a development rights agreement with the land's owner, the Titular Roman Catholic Bishop of Malacca-Johor.</p>
<p>The entire project will cost 476 million ringgit and is expected to be completed by 2002.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
</text>
